course: dictionary
lesson: 13504
title: Immerse: under water or fully absorbed
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To immerse something means to put it completely under water or another liquid. «Mum immersed the eggs in boiling water.» Every egg went right under the water, not just the top.
explain: Immerse also describes your mind. When you are immersed in something, you are so involved in it that you think of nothing else. «Sam was immersed in his book and did not hear the bell.» He did not hear the bell because his mind was on the book.
explain: Look at the words around immersed to find its meaning. Water is a clue for the first meaning, and not hearing the bell is a clue for the second. Check by putting your meaning into the sentence and seeing if it still makes sense.
fact: Immerse is a verb. Its other forms are immerses, immersed and immersing.
fact: «Immerse» means to put something completely under water or another liquid.
fact: «Immersed in» means fully involved in something, so you think of nothing else.
fact: In science, you can immerse an object in water to see whether it floats or sinks.
fact: Learning a language by immersion means living among the language every day.
exercise: «Ravi immersed the sponge in the bucket.» What does immersed mean here? | Thrown away | Dropped on the floor | *Put completely under the water | Squeezed dry
exercise: «She was so immersed in her game that she forgot her dinner.» What does immersed in mean? | Angry with her friends | Bored and tired | Sitting under a table | *Fully involved, thinking of nothing else
exercise: «Tom immersed the stone in a jar of water and watched the level rise.» Why did the water level rise? | *The stone took up space in the water | The stone was hot | The jar was too full of sand | Tom blew on the water
test: «Lena was immersed in her painting for three hours.» What does immersed mean here? | Put under water | *Fully absorbed, thinking of nothing else | Finished early | Very cold
test: Jayden is learning Spanish by immersion, so what is he doing? | *Living among the language every day | Listening to the radio once a month | Writing letters to his teacher | Reading one book each week
exam: «Before the experiment, Ben immersed the rock in the water.» What did Ben do? | Painted the rock blue | Lifted the rock out of the water | *Put the rock completely under the water | Broke the rock into pieces
